    "body": "> (auto generated by Claude)\n\nSplit from #44626 by @YAMY1234 (the sparse decode attention part), without the `--enable-dsv41-low-latency-decode` switch.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `can_use_swapab_attention` takes up to `SM100_MAX_ROWS = 24` rows (was 8). Past 8 rows, SM100 used FlashMLA on 64 zero-padded heads; swap-AB is faster up to 24 rows, and FlashMLA wins from 32.\n- `swapab_attention` launches the split-KV kernel and the combine with PDL (`pdl=True` by default). `partial_gluon` waits before its first load and triggers its dependents after its last global load. The combine waits, then triggers right away, so `fused_rope_wo_a` streams its weights during the combine.\n- Narrow combine (`narrow_combine=True` by default): one-warp programs over 128 columns when there is an extra key range.\n- gfx950 is unchanged: `swapab_gluon_hip` passes `pdl=False, narrow_combine=False` and still dispatches at most 8 rows.\n\n## Accuracy\n\nB300: `test_swapab_attention.py` passes. Ad hoc cases at 1-24 rows (eager and CUDA graph, with and without PDL / narrow combine) match the fp64 reference at the bf16 rounding floor. PDL and the trigger position are bit-identical to the non-PDL path. At 9-24 rows, swap-AB is closer to the reference than FlashMLA (RMS error 1.00x vs 1.27-1.38x the bf16 floor).\n\n## Speed\n\nB300, one CUDA graph of `fused_q_norm_rope` -> attention -> `fused_rope_wo_a_bf16` (all with PDL), cold L2, us, median of 5 processes:\n\n| Rows | main | this PR | Speedup |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 6 | 19.37 | 16.71 | 1.16x |\n| 8 | 19.63 | 16.85 | 1.17x |\n| 12 | 29.14 | 17.28 | 1.69x |\n| 16 | 29.19 | 20.24 | 1.44x |\n| 24 | 29.58 | 21.52 | 1.37x |\n\nPDL alone accounts for 1.6-2.5 us of the chain at every row count. In the end-to-end decode of DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on GB300 (TP4, EP1, DSpark), sparse attention per step drops from 824 to 363 us at batch 2 (12 rows) and from 827 to 519 us at batch 4 (24 rows).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\